The metro arrives, and the doors open.
I go into the train.
The train drives without a driver.
I walk all the way to the front.
I stand by the large window.
I ride with the metro through the dark.
We are in a long tunnel.
We drive very fast.
The light flies past the window.
It looks fantastic.
A little boy stands next to me.
He also looks out into the dark.
I often take the metro.
It is a fast and easy trip.
Now we are approaching my station.
I am going to the harbour.
My next trip is with the harbour bus.
I am looking forward to seeing the water.
